  ('ai:ai-batch-02:bd8511e3a613','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','I came ___ an old photo while I was cleaning the attic.',array['up','through','along','across']::text[],'D','''Come across'' = find by chance.',array['phrasal_verbs']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:8f294436e268','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','We''ve run ___ of milk, so I''m going to the shop.',array['off','away','down','out']::text[],'D','''Run out of'' = have none left.',array['phrasal_verbs']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:ebe3bd7b55a8','B2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','The hotel was expensive; ___, the service was excellent.',array['therefore','as a result','for example','however']::text[],'D','''However'' introduces a contrast.',array['linkers']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:19bf0974b2d4','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','According to the text, what is one advantage of remote work?',array['Work and private life are clearly separated.','New employees learn faster.','Companies pay higher salaries.','People spend less time travelling to work.']::text[],'D','Supporters say it ''saves commuting time''.',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','Remote work, once a rare privilege, has become common in many industries. Supporters argue that it saves commuting time and allows people to organise their day more flexibly. Critics, however, point out that working from home can blur the line between professional and private life, and that new employees in particular may miss out on the informal learning that happens in an office. Some companies have therefore adopted a ''hybrid'' model, in which staff spend part of the week at home and part in the office.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:45e98d1573b5','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','According to critics, who may lose out most from remote work?',array['older staff','new employees','managers','commuters']::text[],'B','''New employees in particular may miss out on the informal learning''.',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','Remote work, once a rare privilege, has become common in many industries. Supporters argue that it saves commuting time and allows people to organise their day more flexibly. Critics, however, point out that working from home can blur the line between professional and private life, and that new employees in particular may miss out on the informal learning that happens in an office. Some companies have therefore adopted a ''hybrid'' model, in which staff spend part of the week at home and part in the office.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:e21a7356f54f','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is a ''hybrid'' model?',array['working at night and at weekends','working only from home','working for two different companies','working partly at home and partly in the office']::text[],'D','''Staff spend part of the week at home and part in the office.''',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','Remote work, once a rare privilege, has become common in many industries. Supporters argue that it saves commuting time and allows people to organise their day more flexibly. Critics, however, point out that working from home can blur the line between professional and private life, and that new employees in particular may miss out on the informal learning that happens in an office. Some companies have therefore adopted a ''hybrid'' model, in which staff spend part of the week at home and part in the office.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:49b144f0dbdf','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','In the text, the word ''blur'' is closest in meaning to ___.',array['make less clear','make stronger','explain','separate']::text[],'A','To blur a line is to make it less clear.',array['reading','vocabulary_in_context']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','Remote work, once a rare privilege, has become common in many industries. Supporters argue that it saves commuting time and allows people to organise their day more flexibly. Critics, however, point out that working from home can blur the line between professional and private life, and that new employees in particular may miss out on the informal learning that happens in an office. Some companies have therefore adopted a ''hybrid'' model, in which staff spend part of the week at home and part in the office.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:42d2d1ad8c20','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is the writer''s overall opinion of the film?',array['mixed, but mostly disappointed','completely negative','completely positive','they have no opinion']::text[],'A','The writer praises the photography and acting but was disappointed overall.',array['reading','attitude']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','I had high hopes for ''The Silent River'', but the film left me disappointed. The photography is breathtaking and the lead actress gives a convincing performance. Unfortunately, the plot is so slow that I kept checking the time, and the ending raises more questions than it answers. Worth watching for the scenery, but don''t expect a gripping story.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:f6fd6e405661','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What did the writer like about the film?',array['the photography and the lead actress','the gripping story','the fast plot','the clear ending']::text[],'A','''The photography is breathtaking and the lead actress gives a convincing performance.''',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','I had high hopes for ''The Silent River'', but the film left me disappointed. The photography is breathtaking and the lead actress gives a convincing performance. Unfortunately, the plot is so slow that I kept checking the time, and the ending raises more questions than it answers. Worth watching for the scenery, but don''t expect a gripping story.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:7c6e3c88301d','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why did the writer keep checking the time?',array['The story moved very slowly.','The cinema was cold.','The writer was late for another film.','The film was too short.']::text[],'A','''The plot is so slow that I kept checking the time.''',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','I had high hopes for ''The Silent River'', but the film left me disappointed. The photography is breathtaking and the lead actress gives a convincing performance. Unfortunately, the plot is so slow that I kept checking the time, and the ending raises more questions than it answers. Worth watching for the scenery, but don''t expect a gripping story.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:d3bb921df61f','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Look at the chart. Which statement is true?',array['Sales rose every month from March to June.','Sales fell steadily over the six months.','Sales were highest in January.','Sales in May were lower than in April.']::text[],'A','March 20, April 30, May 45, June 60: they rose every month.',array['picture','charts']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,'image','samples/sales_chart.png','A bar chart'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:8ab77e7fe3d5','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Watch the video. What happened to the number of visitors between 2020 and 2024?',array['It tripled.','It stayed the same.','It halved.','It doubled.']::text[],'D','From 200,000 to 400,000: twice as many.',array['video','charts']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,'video','samples/museum_visitors.mp4','Museum visitors (6 seconds)'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:cae16265654e','B2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Watch the video. By how much did visitor numbers increase between 2022 and 2024?',array['by 100,000','by 300,000','by 50,000','by 200,000']::text[],'A','300,000 in 2022 and 400,000 in 2024.',array['video','charts','numbers']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,'video','samples/museum_visitors.mp4','Museum visitors (6 seconds)'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:58058c97588f','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Choose the most natural sentence:',array['Hardly no one turned up to the meeting.','Hardly anyone turned up to the meeting.','Hard anyone turned up to the meeting.','Hardly anyone didn''t turn up to the meeting.']::text[],'B','''Hardly'' is already negative, so it takes ''anyone'', not a second negative.',array['negatives','correct_sentence']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:85ec218a7c6c','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Find the mistake: "The number of applicants have risen sharply." Which word is wrong?',array['sharply','number','applicants','have']::text[],'D','''The number of…'' takes a singular verb: has risen.',array['agreement','error_spotting']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:e4a956613a84','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Find the mistake: "She suggested me to apply for the job." Which part is wrong?',array['the job','suggested','me to apply','for']::text[],'C','Say ''suggested that I apply'' or ''suggested applying''.',array['verb_patterns','error_spotting']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:69a1559aac34','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Should you need any help, ___ hesitate to contact us.',array['no','won''t','not','don''t']::text[],'D','Fixed formal phrase: ''Should you need…, don''t hesitate to…''.',array['inversion','formal']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:2579e5f7ce80','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','It''s no use ___ about it now; the decision has been made.',array['to complain','complained','complaining','complain']::text[],'C','''It''s no use'' is followed by -ing.',array['gerunds']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:f878b34ea2dc','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','She is said to ___ fluent Arabic as a child.',array['had spoken','speak','have spoken','be speaking']::text[],'C','Reporting the past: be said to + have + past participle.',array['passive_reporting']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:60e36a5f3e22','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Which phrase is closest in meaning to ''scrutinise''?',array['praise','ignore','examine closely','summarise']::text[],'C','To scrutinise is to examine very carefully.',array['synonyms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:c6c3c3898dc1','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Which phrase is closest in meaning to ''mitigate''?',array['make worse','mention','measure','reduce the harm of']::text[],'D','To mitigate is to make something bad less severe.',array['synonyms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:f7d68c87cde4','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The ___ of the data is questionable. (RELY)',array['reliably','reliance','reliant','reliability']::text[],'D','Reliability = how far something can be trusted.',array['word_formation']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:c88ee3238615','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Her ___ remarks offended several colleagues. (SENSITIVE)',array['sensitively','sensible','insensitive','sensitivity']::text[],'C','Remarks that offend people are insensitive.',array['word_formation']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:78abf0243acb','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The government has ___ a series of measures to tackle unemployment.',array['made up','brought round','set off','introduced']::text[],'D','Collocation: introduce measures.',array['collocations']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:186e500e621d','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','These findings ___ serious doubt on the theory.',array['make','put','give','cast']::text[],'D','Collocation: cast doubt on something.',array['collocations']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:fb4a171b1274','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The negotiations broke ___ after the two sides failed to agree.',array['through','away','in','down']::text[],'D','''Break down'' = fail and stop.',array['phrasal_verbs']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:88eb6a4aeb2c','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','___ his lack of experience, he was offered the job.',array['Although','Whereas','Provided','Notwithstanding']::text[],'D','''Notwithstanding'' (= despite) is followed by a noun phrase.',array['linkers','formal']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:f37986826af7','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Which sentence has the right register for a formal letter?',array['Just wanted to ask about that job.','I am writing to enquire about the position advertised.','I''m writing to ask about the job you put up.','Hey, is the job still free?']::text[],'B','Formal letters avoid contractions and informal phrases.',array['register','writing']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:9111d2efa86c','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','According to the passage, multitasking is actually ___.',array['doing two things truly at the same time','the best way to save time','quick switching between tasks','a skill most people master with practice']::text[],'C','''…is, in reality, rapid switching between tasks''.',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','The assumption that multitasking boosts productivity has been increasingly called into question. Studies in cognitive psychology suggest that what we perceive as doing several things at once is, in reality, rapid switching between tasks, each switch carrying a small but measurable cost in time and accuracy. Paradoxically, people who consider themselves skilled multitaskers often perform worse on tests of attention than those who rarely multitask. Rather than abandoning multitasking entirely, researchers advocate ''batching'' similar tasks together to minimise the number of switches.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:d1ac287f9a00','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is paradoxical about people who think they multitask well?',array['They tend to do worse on attention tests.','They sleep less than others.','They never switch tasks.','They are better at batching.']::text[],'A','They ''often perform worse on tests of attention''.',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','The assumption that multitasking boosts productivity has been increasingly called into question. Studies in cognitive psychology suggest that what we perceive as doing several things at once is, in reality, rapid switching between tasks, each switch carrying a small but measurable cost in time and accuracy. Paradoxically, people who consider themselves skilled multitaskers often perform worse on tests of attention than those who rarely multitask. Rather than abandoning multitasking entirely, researchers advocate ''batching'' similar tasks together to minimise the number of switches.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:18908eda4a54','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What do the researchers recommend?',array['giving up all multitasking','grouping similar tasks together','switching tasks more often','taking longer breaks']::text[],'B','They advocate ''batching'' similar tasks together.',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','The assumption that multitasking boosts productivity has been increasingly called into question. Studies in cognitive psychology suggest that what we perceive as doing several things at once is, in reality, rapid switching between tasks, each switch carrying a small but measurable cost in time and accuracy. Paradoxically, people who consider themselves skilled multitaskers often perform worse on tests of attention than those who rarely multitask. Rather than abandoning multitasking entirely, researchers advocate ''batching'' similar tasks together to minimise the number of switches.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:c9d93785aa23','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','The phrase ''called into question'' is closest in meaning to ___.',array['ignored','doubted','confirmed','advertised']::text[],'B','To call something into question is to doubt it.',array['reading','vocabulary_in_context']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','The assumption that multitasking boosts productivity has been increasingly called into question. Studies in cognitive psychology suggest that what we perceive as doing several things at once is, in reality, rapid switching between tasks, each switch carrying a small but measurable cost in time and accuracy. Paradoxically, people who consider themselves skilled multitaskers often perform worse on tests of attention than those who rarely multitask. Rather than abandoning multitasking entirely, researchers advocate ''batching'' similar tasks together to minimise the number of switches.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:1458817c4f73','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is the main point of the passage about rooftop gardens?',array['They always save water.','Their benefits depend on how they are designed.','Older buildings are ideal for them.','They should be banned in dry cities.']::text[],'B','''Yet their benefits depend heavily on design.''',array['reading','main_idea']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','Urban rooftop gardens are often praised for cooling buildings and providing fresh produce. Yet their benefits depend heavily on design. A shallow layer of soil, for instance, offers little insulation and dries out quickly in summer, requiring frequent watering, which in dry cities may cancel out the environmental gains. Deeper systems perform better but add considerable weight, so many older buildings cannot support them without costly reinforcement.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:98f812c7f000','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why might shallow gardens be a problem in dry cities?',array['They are too heavy.','They need a lot of watering.','They are too expensive to build.','They make buildings hotter.']::text[],'B','Shallow soil ''dries out quickly… requiring frequent watering''.',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','Urban rooftop gardens are often praised for cooling buildings and providing fresh produce. Yet their benefits depend heavily on design. A shallow layer of soil, for instance, offers little insulation and dries out quickly in summer, requiring frequent watering, which in dry cities may cancel out the environmental gains. Deeper systems perform better but add considerable weight, so many older buildings cannot support them without costly reinforcement.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:9b9b04e0efb9','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What is the drawback of deeper systems?',array['their low cost','their weight','their constant need for water','their poor insulation']::text[],'B','Deeper systems ''add considerable weight''.',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','Urban rooftop gardens are often praised for cooling buildings and providing fresh produce. Yet their benefits depend heavily on design. A shallow layer of soil, for instance, offers little insulation and dries out quickly in summer, requiring frequent watering, which in dry cities may cancel out the environmental gains. Deeper systems perform better but add considerable weight, so many older buildings cannot support them without costly reinforcement.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:213e6409f33b','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which description of the chart is most accurate?',array['Sales grew steadily throughout the period.','Sales remained broadly stable.','After a dip in the first quarter, sales recovered strongly.','Sales peaked in January and then declined.']::text[],'C','Sales fell from 40 to 20 (Jan–Mar), then rose to 60 by June.',array['picture','charts','describing_trends']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,'image','samples/sales_chart.png','A bar chart'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:ff5cf1e2d88f','C1'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Watch the video. Which sentence best describes the trend?',array['Visitor numbers remained flat throughout.','Visitor numbers rose steadily, doubling over four years.','Visitor numbers fluctuated wildly.','Visitor numbers peaked in 2022 before falling.']::text[],'B','200 → 300 → 400 thousand: a steady rise that doubles the total.',array['video','charts','describing_trends']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,'video','samples/museum_visitors.mp4','Museum visitors (6 seconds)'),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:28d39d19af2b','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Choose the most idiomatic sentence:',array['The proposal was put on the shelf for being.','The proposal was shelved for the time being.','The proposal was shelving for the time being.','The proposal was shelved for the being time.']::text[],'B','''Shelve'' = postpone; ''for the time being'' = for now.',array['idioms','correct_sentence']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:1d26779203bc','C2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Find the mistake: "Scarcely had the meeting begun than the fire alarm went off." Which word is wrong?',array['Scarcely','had','than','went off']::text[],'C','The pattern is ''Scarcely… when''; ''than'' goes with ''No sooner''.',array['inversion','error_spotting']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:fbe92e927681','C2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','No sooner ___ the contract than the company went bankrupt.',array['did they signed','had they signed','they had signed','they signed']::text[],'B','''No sooner'' at the start needs inversion: had they signed.',array['inversion']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:9e53c4555010','C2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Rarely ___ such a compelling argument been made.',array['did','had been','is','has']::text[],'D','Inversion with the present perfect passive: has … been made.',array['inversion']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:64cb7a9b6944','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The minister was accused of being ___ with the truth.',array['frugal','thrifty','economic','economical']::text[],'D','''Economical with the truth'' is an idiom meaning not telling the whole truth.',array['idioms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:10ba19a82504','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Which phrase is closest in meaning to ''obfuscate''?',array['delay','make obvious','make unclear','exaggerate']::text[],'C','To obfuscate is to make something deliberately unclear.',array['synonyms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:3cc74e1b3aa3','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Which phrase is closest in meaning to ''ubiquitous''?',array['highly valuable','found everywhere','very old','extremely rare']::text[],'B','Ubiquitous = present everywhere.',array['synonyms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:ac10400613af','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Which word is closest in meaning to ''sanguine'' (about the future)?',array['exhausted','optimistic','indifferent','furious']::text[],'B','Sanguine = cheerfully optimistic.',array['synonyms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:119a6502595c','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The ___ of the evidence led to the case being dismissed. (SUFFICIENT)',array['insufficiency','sufficiency','insufficient','sufficiently']::text[],'A','A noun meaning ''not enough'' is needed: insufficiency.',array['word_formation']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:ca0ece75f54e','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','His argument was full of ___. (CONSISTENT)',array['consistency','inconsistent','consistently','inconsistencies']::text[],'D','''Full of'' needs a plural noun: inconsistencies.',array['word_formation']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:9d0aa84eef4a','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','After weeks of arguing, they finally decided to bury the ___.',array['knife','hatchet','hammer','sword']::text[],'B','''Bury the hatchet'' = make peace.',array['idioms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:f29a98c30ecc','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The new manager is a breath of fresh ___.',array['spring','air','wind','sky']::text[],'B','''A breath of fresh air'' = someone new and refreshing.',array['idioms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:3cf431800b81','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The decision was met with ___ criticism from all sides.',array['thick','steep','fierce','tall']::text[],'C','Collocation: fierce criticism.',array['collocations']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:18128b6f00df','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Which is the most formal way to say ''get rid of''?',array['bin','dispose of','ditch','chuck out']::text[],'B','''Dispose of'' is formal; the others are informal.',array['register']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:8766e56a8fb9','C2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Which sentence expresses the strongest certainty about the past?',array['She may have left already.','She might have left already.','She could have left already.','She must have left already.']::text[],'D','''Must have'' = almost certain; might/could/may = possible.',array['modals_past']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:802c528607fa','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What criticism was made of early intelligence tests?',array['They were designed by untrained psychologists.','They measured too many separate abilities.','They favoured people familiar with the test-makers'' culture.','They were too short to be reliable.']::text[],'C','Critics said the tests ''rewarded familiarity with the culture of those who designed them''.',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','Few concepts have proved as slippery as ''intelligence''. Early psychometricians, armed with batteries of tests, assumed they were measuring a single, general capacity; critics countered that such tests merely rewarded familiarity with the culture of those who designed them. More recent theorists have splintered the notion into multiple intelligences (linguistic, spatial, interpersonal and so on), a move hailed by some as liberating and dismissed by others as so elastic as to be meaningless. What is not in dispute is that the way a society defines intelligence reveals as much about its values as about the minds it seeks to measure.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:b497b24e4c92','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Why do some people dismiss the idea of multiple intelligences?',array['They think it is too broad to mean anything.','They believe no tests could be designed for it.','They think it is too narrow.','They think it ignores spatial ability.']::text[],'A','It is dismissed ''as so elastic as to be meaningless''.',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','Few concepts have proved as slippery as ''intelligence''. Early psychometricians, armed with batteries of tests, assumed they were measuring a single, general capacity; critics countered that such tests merely rewarded familiarity with the culture of those who designed them. More recent theorists have splintered the notion into multiple intelligences (linguistic, spatial, interpersonal and so on), a move hailed by some as liberating and dismissed by others as so elastic as to be meaningless. What is not in dispute is that the way a society defines intelligence reveals as much about its values as about the minds it seeks to measure.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:a5a87f8ced25','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','Which statement reflects the author''s final point?',array['Definitions of intelligence reveal a society''s values.','Intelligence cannot be measured at all.','The theory of multiple intelligences is correct.','General intelligence is the only valid concept.']::text[],'A','The way a society defines intelligence ''reveals as much about its values''.',array['reading','main_idea']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','Few concepts have proved as slippery as ''intelligence''. Early psychometricians, armed with batteries of tests, assumed they were measuring a single, general capacity; critics countered that such tests merely rewarded familiarity with the culture of those who designed them. More recent theorists have splintered the notion into multiple intelligences (linguistic, spatial, interpersonal and so on), a move hailed by some as liberating and dismissed by others as so elastic as to be meaningless. What is not in dispute is that the way a society defines intelligence reveals as much about its values as about the minds it seeks to measure.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:7f64a36933eb','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','In the passage, ''slippery'' means ___.',array['dangerous to use','easy to measure','hard to define precisely','widely accepted']::text[],'C','A slippery concept is hard to pin down.',array['reading','vocabulary_in_context']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','Few concepts have proved as slippery as ''intelligence''. Early psychometricians, armed with batteries of tests, assumed they were measuring a single, general capacity; critics countered that such tests merely rewarded familiarity with the culture of those who designed them. More recent theorists have splintered the notion into multiple intelligences (linguistic, spatial, interpersonal and so on), a move hailed by some as liberating and dismissed by others as so elastic as to be meaningless. What is not in dispute is that the way a society defines intelligence reveals as much about its values as about the minds it seeks to measure.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:a039549f73f2','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','How did shopkeepers first react to the plan?',array['They welcomed it enthusiastically.','They asked for higher rents.','They proposed it to the council.','They opposed it, fearing a loss of business.']::text[],'D','There was ''a chorus of objections… who predicted a collapse in trade''.',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','The town council''s decision to pedestrianise the old quarter was greeted with a chorus of objections from shopkeepers, who predicted a collapse in trade. Two years on, footfall has risen by a third, and several of the most vocal opponents now concede that their fears were misplaced, though they are quick to add that rents have climbed accordingly, pricing some long-standing businesses out of the area.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:413d1834fc53','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What has happened to the number of visitors to the old quarter?',array['It has stayed the same.','It has tripled.','It has fallen by a third.','It has risen by about a third.']::text[],'D','''Footfall has risen by a third.''',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','The town council''s decision to pedestrianise the old quarter was greeted with a chorus of objections from shopkeepers, who predicted a collapse in trade. Two years on, footfall has risen by a third, and several of the most vocal opponents now concede that their fears were misplaced, though they are quick to add that rents have climbed accordingly, pricing some long-standing businesses out of the area.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:f0500c75e0db','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','What new problem do the shopkeepers point out?',array['The council has closed several shops.','There are now too few visitors.','Rising rents are forcing some businesses out.','Cars still enter the old quarter.']::text[],'C','''Rents have climbed accordingly, pricing some long-standing businesses out.''',array['reading']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','The town council''s decision to pedestrianise the old quarter was greeted with a chorus of objections from shopkeepers, who predicted a collapse in trade. Two years on, footfall has risen by a third, and several of the most vocal opponents now concede that their fears were misplaced, though they are quick to add that rents have climbed accordingly, pricing some long-standing businesses out of the area.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:fc2cde4f2809','C2'::public.cefr_level,'reading','''Their fears were misplaced'' means the fears were ___.',array['shared by everyone','unjustified','deliberately exaggerated','hidden']::text[],'B','Misplaced fears turned out to be wrong.',array['reading','vocabulary_in_context']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02','The town council''s decision to pedestrianise the old quarter was greeted with a chorus of objections from shopkeepers, who predicted a collapse in trade. Two years on, footfall has risen by a third, and several of the most vocal opponents now concede that their fears were misplaced, though they are quick to add that rents have climbed accordingly, pricing some long-standing businesses out of the area.',null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:cc8e23c17c9a','B1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','A: Shall we go to the cinema tonight?  B: ___',array['I''d love to, but I have to study.','I''d love going, but I have studied.','Yes, we shall went.','No, we didn''t.']::text[],'A','A polite refusal with a reason.',array['dialogue','invitations']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:c7f4e8a72b6f','B1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','I''ve never been to Paris, and my sister hasn''t ___.',array['also','either','neither','too']::text[],'B','In negative sentences we use ''either'' at the end.',array['agreement']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:c23b3e7edc4e','B1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','If I were you, I ___ apply for that job.',array['will','did','would','am']::text[],'C','Advice: If I were you, I would…',array['conditionals','advice']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:a84257ea775d','B1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','This is the town ___ I grew up.',array['which','who','what','where']::text[],'D','''Where'' refers to a place in relative clauses.',array['relative_clauses']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:ead5fe2b50c8','B1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Which word is closest in meaning to ''purchase''?',array['borrow','return','sell','buy']::text[],'D','To purchase = to buy.',array['synonyms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:d5f6441b4feb','B1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Sorry I''m late. I got stuck in ___ traffic.',array['heavy','hard','fat','thick']::text[],'A','Collocation: heavy traffic.',array['collocations']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:d29cf7b4b42d','B1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','She ___ her driving test on her first attempt.',array['achieved','succeeded','passed','won']::text[],'C','Collocation: pass a test.',array['collocations']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:96631b344c43','B1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','My phone needs ___. The battery is almost empty.',array['charging','be charging','charge','charged']::text[],'A','''Need + -ing'' has a passive meaning: it needs to be charged.',array['gerunds']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:877552eb4c13','B1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','We had to ___ the match because of the storm, so it never happened.',array['call back','call off','call up','call in']::text[],'B','''Call off'' = cancel.',array['phrasal_verbs']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:5837aacf2ca8','B1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Find the mistake: "If it will rain tomorrow, we''ll stay at home." Which word is wrong?',array['If','will','stay','rain']::text[],'B','After ''if'' we use the present: If it rains…',array['conditionals','error_spotting']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:9a4980685dde','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','A: Could you possibly lend me your laptop?  B: ___',array['No problem, I borrowed it.','Yes, I lend.','Sure, as long as you''re careful with it.','Sure, I could possibly.']::text[],'C','Agreeing with a condition: as long as…',array['dialogue','requests']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:76cc9165037c','B2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','I''d rather ___ at home tonight.',array['to stay','staying','stayed','stay']::text[],'D','''Would rather'' + base form for your own preference.',array['preferences']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:10c9f4bc60f2','B2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','She was the first woman ___ the prize.',array['to win','winning','won','who win']::text[],'A','''The first/last/only'' + to-infinitive.',array['infinitives']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:59456e3d31ac','B2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Which phrase is closest in meaning to ''put up with''?',array['build','support financially','postpone','tolerate']::text[],'D','To put up with = to tolerate.',array['phrasal_verbs','synonyms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:1152183338a5','B2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','There''s no point ___ to persuade him; he never changes his mind.',array['tried','to try','try','trying']::text[],'D','''There''s no point'' + -ing.',array['gerunds']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:6e23e3e66adc','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Not until I got home ___ that I had lost my keys.',array['I realised','did I realise','I did realise','had I realised']::text[],'B','''Not until…'' at the start: inversion in the main clause (did I realise).',array['inversion']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:154d828570e9','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','The proposal was rejected ___ the grounds that it was too expensive.',array['for','in','on','at']::text[],'C','Fixed phrase: on the grounds that.',array['prepositions','formal']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:62fe5ae53f14','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Which phrase is closest in meaning to ''a foregone conclusion''?',array['an unexpected result','a long debate','a forgotten decision','a certain outcome']::text[],'D','A foregone conclusion is a result that is certain in advance.',array['idioms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:984ef166eb7a','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','She has a ___ for languages; she speaks five fluently.',array['fluency','flare','flair','flavour']::text[],'C','''A flair for'' = a natural talent for.',array['collocations']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:e9c0a42eb358','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Find the mistake: "Each of the students have submitted their essay." Which word is wrong?',array['submitted','Each','essay','have']::text[],'D','''Each of…'' takes a singular verb: has submitted.',array['agreement','error_spotting']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:fb4cea72c455','C1'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The two companies are ___ talks about a possible merger.',array['holding','doing','making','keeping']::text[],'A','Collocation: hold talks.',array['collocations']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:56a0c85b9a96','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Choose the sentence that uses ''whom'' correctly:',array['Whom do you think is right?','Whom is calling, please?','The man whom lives next door is a pilot.','To whom should I address the letter?']::text[],'D','''Whom'' is an object form; after a preposition it is correct.',array['relative_clauses','formal']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:4632616d460f','C1'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','You may borrow the car ___ you return it by six.',array['provided that','even though','whereas','so that']::text[],'A','''Provided that'' introduces a condition.',array['linkers','conditionals']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:09b08c9bbbfd','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Which word is closest in meaning to ''ephemeral''?',array['everlasting','fragile','imaginary','short-lived']::text[],'D','Ephemeral = lasting a very short time.',array['synonyms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:f341107b5e79','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','His remarks were ___ to the point of rudeness.',array['blunt','tactful','verbose','oblique']::text[],'A','Blunt = very direct, without trying to be polite.',array['adjectives']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:f7e06abd1fc0','C2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Had it not been for her help, we ___ the deadline.',array['would miss','would have missed','will have missed','had missed']::text[],'B','Inverted third conditional: Had it not been for…, would have + past participle.',array['inversion','conditionals']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:d84dde82ddd3','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','That''s a red ___; it has nothing to do with the real issue.',array['herring','carpet','fish','flag']::text[],'A','A red herring distracts from the real issue.',array['idioms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:4d103406b0f8','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The evidence is ___; it could support either interpretation.',array['conclusive','equivocal','irrefutable','unequivocal']::text[],'B','Equivocal = open to more than one interpretation.',array['advanced_adjectives']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:2be59f5d3231','C2'::public.cefr_level,'grammar','Find the mistake: "Hardly had I sat down when the phone rings." Which word is wrong?',array['sat','had','Hardly','rings']::text[],'D','The sentence is in the past: the phone rang.',array['inversion','error_spotting']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:425cacce87b1','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','Which is the most formal way to say ''look into the matter''?',array['check out the matter','sort out the matter','dig into the matter','investigate the matter']::text[],'D','''Investigate'' is the formal equivalent.',array['register']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null),
  ('ai:ai-batch-02:117fce276a43','C2'::public.cefr_level,'vocabulary','The government''s response was criticised as too little, too ___.',array['slow','late','soon','small']::text[],'B','Fixed phrase: too little, too late.',array['idioms']::text[],'draft','unreviewed','ai-draft:ai-batch-02',null,null,null,null)
on conflict (external_ref) do update set
  cefr_level = excluded.cefr_level, skill = excluded.skill, prompt = excluded.prompt,
  options = excluded.options, correct_option = excluded.correct_option,
  explanation = excluded.explanation, tags = excluded.tags, passage = excluded.passage,
  media_type = excluded.media_type, media_path = excluded.media_path, media_caption = excluded.media_caption
where public.assessment_questions.status = 'draft' and public.assessment_questions.review_status = 'unreviewed';
